From 8b79d3cca450fe1be272e378ce121bafa30ab38b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VortaForge Archival <archival@vortaforge.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:18:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chore(datapacks)!: retire the datapack programme, arm the
 guard, make the repository English-only

One squashed change set from a clean pre-retirement `main`, so the series
applies with a single `git am` and never carries intermediate Turkish text in
and then back out.

  * Every datapack, resource pack, generator, linter and test harness moves to
    `archived/` with `git mv` (renames preserved, 3546 paths).
  * The datapack Gradle logic is extracted from the root `build.gradle` into six
    separate files under `archived/build/`, with a line-range probe
    (`probe.lock`); the root build no longer registers pack tasks.
  * `archived/archive.json` is rebuilt as schema v2: 28 entries, every one
    `"disarmed": true`, each with a reason.
  * The kill switch is `datapacks.disabled.json` (`"enabled": false`), fail
    closed on a missing file, with a token-gated CLI
    (`scripts/datapacks_disable.py`).
  * `scripts/datapack_guard.py` refuses new datapack content, revived archived
    tooling and blocklisted accounts from pre-commit, pre-push, CI and Gradle.
  * `blocklist/blocklist.json` blocks verified datapack tooling authors by
    login and numeric id; the maintainers sit in `managed.accounts`.
  * English only: no Turkish in the live tree, in script output or in the
    registry. `archived/packs/` keeps its frozen upstream translations.

Verified on the applied tree: check_archive 28/0/0, kill switch 0 problems,
watermarks 15/11, 84 Python tests, the Node site test, and Gradle 9.8.2 with
guardArchives checkDatapackSwitch checkArchive verifyMod testRepository.
